UID:2c65fe3a809df8d4200de582c12f1b38@visitsantarosa.com
DESCRIPTION:Asemic writing is the creation of marks that resemble handwrit
 ing but carry no literal meaning or readable text. It is the word before w
 ords form—the voice too distant to be understood—a universal expressio
 n without country or dialect. We’ll begin with a slideshow exploring the
  rich history and possibilities of asemic writing\, from ancient scripts a
 nd symbols to the calligraphic line and the work of contemporary artists. 
 From there\, you’ll begin your own exploration using ink\, watercolor\, 
 and a 
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\,  282 S. High Street\, Sebastopol
 \, CA 95472
